# This file tells Git which files and folders to IGNORE when tracking
# changes. Anything listed here will NOT be saved in the project's
# version history. This is important for security and cleanliness.

# --- PROJECT CONTEXT ---
# This is the gitignore for a macOS backup/restore toolkit. We need to
# exclude backup folders because they contain sensitive SSH private keys
# that should never be committed to version control.

# Ignore all backup snapshot folders. The pattern "Mac_Backup_*/" matches
# any folder whose name starts with "Mac_Backup_" followed by anything
# (like a date). These folders contain SSH private keys — secret files
# that let your computer authenticate with servers like GitHub. If these
# were committed to a public repository, anyone could steal your identity
# online. The trailing slash means "only match directories, not files."
Mac_Backup_*/

# Ignore all .bak files. These are backup copies of configuration files
# (like .zshrc.bak) that are created during the backup process. They
# are working files that don't belong in version control.
*.bak

# Ignore macOS system files. ".DS_Store" is a hidden file that macOS
# automatically creates in every folder you open in Finder. It stores
# display settings like icon positions and folder views. It has nothing
# to do with the project and clutters up the repository with unnecessary
# changes every time someone opens the folder on a Mac.
.DS_Store
